## Stage Research

The original `project-context/AGENT_SESSION_DELEGATION_REENTRY.md` decision remains **NARROW** for the bounded first consumer.

Material hardening re-entries are recorded in:

- `project-context/AGENT_SESSION_BROWSER_RECOVERY_HARDENING.md` — provider-conversation recovery identity, browser claim ownership, delivery/capture crash recovery and multi-monitor cleanup/capture authority;
- `project-context/AGENT_SESSION_PROFILE_BOUNDARY_REENTRY.md` — generic worker-profile identity must not make Temporary Chat freshness universal.

Generic delegation stores a bounded `worker_profile` identifier as part of deterministic identity, while each provider adapter owns support/qualification policy. No rich-context worker, Prime integration, registry, scheduler, mutating child or additional provider is introduced here.

## Generic lifecycle

The PR provides deterministic provider-independent delegation identity, immutable private genesis/run capability, separate durable delivery identity, crash-safe state, one-shot launch/delivery claims, exact child/session binding, `prepared | claimed | unknown | delivered`, no blind re-Send, same-delivery reconciliation and one exact bounded terminal result.

## First physical adapter — `chatgpt-temporary`

The current adapter remains strictly `fresh_readonly_worker_v1` and rejects any other bounded profile before durable launch authority is committed. Temporary Chat remains first-adapter/profile policy, not universal Agent Session truth.

## Latest fresh-review hardening

The fresh ordinary-ChatGPT review on exact HEAD `3e0ecd2438d96e48bc404bf041d5ba17f26c891e` reported three findings. Development-side falsification independently confirmed all three:

1. a tab that lost the IndexedDB claim race could still recover project-local pre-Send authority while durable delivery remained `prepared`;
2. a durable delivered commit followed by HTTP acknowledgement loss could wedge the browser because retries changed `evidence_ref` and local state could not reconcile from controller status;
3. a controller/network interruption during final capture could stop the content loop instead of re-arming and reconciling terminal durable state.

Current fixes now:

- require the exact persisted `claim_tab_id` owner before the existing-claim/prepared path may request local Send authority;
- keep one stable delivery evidence identity across retries of the same observed outcome and serialize delivery POSTs;
- reconcile authoritative `delivery_state` and terminal `result_state` from authenticated `/status` even while local delivery state is stale;
- treat capture transport interruption as recoverable authority loss, invalidate local capture authority, require the clean interval again after recovery, and close from terminal durable status if capture committed before acknowledgement loss;
- include focused Node-backed adversarial regressions for all three cases.

An intermediate CI run exposed a defect only in the new browser-claim regression harness: VM-scoped controller-status fixtures referenced host-only correlation variables. The harness now explicitly exposes those values into the VM context while retaining the exact owner/loser authority assertions. The corrected exact-head `ci` passes the complete Python/controller/vision contract suite.

The `3e0ecd...` review is **STALE** for merge acceptance because its findings were fixed by later commits.

